  <rdf:Description rdf:nodeID="commodity_genet_cb1040dd375129257158428e7308c34d72a6788b914ff2c358a92e9402ce0802b01">
    <crm:P190_has_symbolic_content>the genet (also jenet), a kind of civet-cat native to southern Europe, west Asia and Africa; (pl.) the skins of the animal employed as fur for garments (Veale 219). Black skins were more valuable than grey; the best were taken in season, i.e. killed in winter when the animal is normally hunted (Veale 25).</crm:P190_has_symbolic_content>
    <crm:P2_has_type rdf:resource="http://vocab.getty.edu/aat/300435416"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.cidoc-crm.org/cidoc-crm/E33_Linguistic_Object"/>
  </rdf:Description>
</rdf:RDF>
